### VS Code ###
.vscode/

# Excludes for npm
node_modules
node

# Log output from local tooling (e.g. ttcli) -- never contains anything worth
# committing, only personal paths/noise.
*.log

# Claude Code's local configuration. settings.local.json can accumulate real
# secrets from local testing (API tokens, bcrypt hashes used against a dev
# server) inside its Bash permission allow-list, and the rest is per-machine
# tooling state rather than anything a contributor needs.
/.claude/

### Docker deployment (install.sh / docker-compose.yml) ###
# .env holds real secrets (API token, bcrypt hash) and must never be committed.
.env
# install.sh writes these when you choose to reconfigure; they carry the same secrets.
.env.bak.*
# A copy of the jar for the container to mount -- not an artifact worth storing.
/itemforge.jar
# World and config of the Paper server running under Docker, including the
# config.yml that carries the real token.
/server-data/
# Dashboard container data: the reference texture library an admin imported
# (their resource packs, not assets belonging to this project).
/dashboard-data/

### Internal working documents ###
# Architecture notes, coding standards and test plans, plus the CLAUDE.md that
# indexes them. Kept local: they describe how the project is built rather than
# how it is used, and README.md is the entry point for anyone cloning the repo.
# The pattern is /docs/* rather than /docs/ because git cannot re-include a
# path whose parent directory is itself ignored.
/docs/*
/CLAUDE.md
# The one public part of docs/: screenshots and GIFs linked from README.md.
!/docs/showcase/
